# These are pinned inputs, so they must come out of a checkout as the same bytes
# that went in. Without this, Git's autocrlf rewrote the line endings of the GML
# on checkout and turned 68,517 bytes into 69,950 — and a fixture whose length
# depends on the machine that checked it out is not pinned.
# `docs/work/.gitattributes` does the same thing for the same reason.
* -text
